      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`_generate_loop` builds the client error with `str(e).splitlines()[0]`. For an exception with an empty message, this raises `IndexError` inside the `except` block:\n\n- the client gets no `error` message, the socket just closes;\n- the original exception is lost, because `generate()` only logs the task's exception at debug level through `_await_realtime_task`;\n- `pending_send_task` is never awaited, so a chunk still being sent is left running while the session is cleaned up.\n\nAn empty message is easy to hit. `BaseRealtimeModelAdapter.sample_chunk_inputs` and `build_sampling_params` raise a bare `NotImplementedError`, so an adapter that misses one of them fails this way.\n\nA message that starts with a newline does not crash, but the client receives `error during generate loop: ` with no reason.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `_first_error_line`, which returns the first non-blank line of the message, or the exception class name when there is none.\n- Add a regression case for both failures to `test_realtime_runtime.py`. It fails on `main` (`IndexError`, then an empty reason) and passes with this change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo change to model code or outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nOnly the error path changes. No GPU was used for this PR.\n\n- `test/unit/realtime/test_realtime_runtime.py`: 45 passed on CPU (macOS arm64, Python 3.13, torch 2.15.0).\n- Over a real socket (uvicorn and a `websockets` client, with an adapter that reaches the bare `NotImplementedError`):\n\n| | Client receives |\n|---|---|\n| `main` | nothing, the connection drops |\n| This PR | `{\"type\": \"error\", \"content\": \"error during generate loop: NotImplementedError\"}`, then the connection drops |\n\nThe connection still ends without a close frame after an error, as it does for every other generate loop failure. I left that out of this PR.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the pre-commit hooks (isort 7.0.0, ruff 0.15.1, codespell 2.4.1 on the two changed files).\n- [x] Add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation as needed (not needed).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results (not needed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41791249843](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41791249843)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41791250013](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41791250013)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41791250027](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41791250027)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
